  "upstream_context": "The pathname APIs can follow attacker-replaced symlink components when called with authority over a target file. Upstream acl 2.4.0 adds directory-relative APIs; callers must adopt them where needed. Upgrading the library alone does not make legacy pathname callers safe. Debian trixie still lists acl 2.3.2-2 as vulnerable at this review date.",
