  "conclusion": "Five installed utilities (cp, install, mv, sed and tar) import affected pathname functions. useradd and usermod link libacl and import perm_copy_fd, without direct imports of the four affected functions. No inspected trusted module import mapped libacl, and no invocation of these utilities or ACL functions was identified in the reviewed Chipload runtime paths. Untrusted source can call these utilities or load libacl inside its existing worker authority; it has no host or trusted-service storage mount. This does not add authority over trusted repository files under the supplied launch policy.",
  "limitations": [
    "The vulnerable library and utility callers remain installed. Keep the raw package finding; no scanner suppression or package-fix claim is made.",
    "Import snapshots do not execute every service path. ELF string and symbol inspection do not prove the absence of statically embedded implementations, computed library names or future late loading.",
    "The conclusion depends on the recorded images, SDK, dependencies, entrypoints and container boundaries. Reassess after any relevant change.",
    "Optional geometry/dependency images, operator host tools, altered entrypoints, privileged debugging and host packages are outside this review.",
    "The broker Docker socket remains host authority; this finding does not qualify unrelated customers to share its host."
  ]
}
